<div class="text-center py-5">
  <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold"><%= ENV.fetch("APP_NAME", "BookClubFever Demo") %></h1>
  <p class="lead text-muted mt-2"><%= ENV.fetch("APP_TAGLINE", "") %></p>
  <p class="text-muted mx-auto mt-3" style="max-width: 620px;">
    Hosting the book club tonight and the room might go quiet? Tell it the book, how far the meeting covers, and
    what people have been saying. You get five openers that are easy to say out loud, a spoiler-free line for the
    group chat, and three books to read next. Nothing past your chapter, no reviews, and never a word about who
    hasn&rsquo;t finished.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-4 d-flex justify-content-center gap-3">
    <% if signed_in? %>
      <%= link_to "Go to my books", book_picks_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
    <% else %>
      <%= link_to "Try it free", sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
      <%= link_to "Sign in", sign_in_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary btn-lg" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<hr class="my-5 opacity-25">

<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 860px;">
  <h2 class="h5 text-muted text-center mb-4">Example &mdash; a fictional library club, ten chapters into <em>Frankenstein</em></h2>

  <div class="card book-spine mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
      <p class="text-muted small mb-1">What the host typed</p>
      <p class="mb-2"><strong>Frankenstein</strong> by Mary Shelley &middot; up to the end of chapter 10 &middot; mixed club</p>
      <p class="mb-0 fst-italic">
        &ldquo;First meeting. A few people said Victor is impossible to like. One person loved Walton&rsquo;s
        letters at the start and nobody else did.&rdquo;
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="boundary-line mb-3"><strong>Spoiler boundary:</strong> Stays within chapters 1 to 10.</p>

  <div class="card opener-card mb-2">
    <div class="card-body d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-3">
      <p class="opener-question mb-0">Some of you find Victor impossible to like; is that a flaw in the book, or the whole point of it?</p>
      <span class="badge angle-badge flex-shrink-0">disagreement</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card opener-card mb-2">
    <div class="card-body d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-3">
      <p class="opener-question mb-0">We hear all of this through Walton&rsquo;s letters before Victor says a word; why do you think Shelley wrapped it in someone else&rsquo;s voice?</p>
      <span class="badge angle-badge flex-shrink-0">craft</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card opener-card mb-3">
    <div class="card-body d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-3">
      <p class="opener-question mb-0">Victor hides his work from everyone who loves him; have you ever kept a project to yourself until it felt too big to share?</p>
      <span class="badge angle-badge flex-shrink-0">personal</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="text-muted small text-center mb-4">&hellip; plus two more openers, each with a follow-up question.</p>

  <div class="row g-4 small">
    <div class="col-md-6">
      <h3 class="h6">For the group chat</h3>
      <blockquote class="spoiler-free mb-0">Chapter 10 ends on a glacier with a conversation you will want to talk about on Thursday.</blockquote>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6">
      <h3 class="h6">Read next</h3>
      <ul class="mb-0">
        <li><em>Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde</em>, Robert Louis Stevenson</li>
        <li><em>The Island of Doctor Moreau</em>, H. G. Wells</li>
        <li><em>Dracula</em>, Bram Stoker</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-center text-muted small mt-4">
    AI-generated. A host&rsquo;s starting point, not a reading guide: check any plot detail against the book.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="text-center mt-5 pb-4">
  <% unless signed_in? %>
    <%= link_to "Get openers for your club &rarr;".html_safe, sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
  <% end %>
  <div class="mt-3 text-muted small">
    Open source &middot;
    <a href="https://bookclubfever.com" class="text-muted">BookClubFever</a>
  </div>
</div>
